  partName: Fuel Pump
  description: The Fuel Pump is a medium-sized, elongated component located at the
    top-left-front of the rocket engine, constructed from a Pompe material. Its primary
    function is to supply fuel to the engine's combustion chamber at the required
    pressure and flow rate, making it a vital component in the engine's fuel system.
    An interesting detail about the Fuel Pump is that it must be designed to operate
    efficiently across a wide range of engine speeds and fuel pressures.
